 "method": {
  "data_source": "ball_balance_v2_results.json",
  "state_extraction": "onset x/v are NOT logged as fields; recovered by regex from the verbatim logged prompt strings (Arm R: catch prompt, issued at onset; Arm D: decider prompt \u2014 its catch prompts are post-decider states and were not used as onset states).",
  "observation": "onset state propagated 0.25 s through the v2 plant (spine PID active, gust on) = the oracle's one-observation moment. Gust accel +/-0.9 taken from the logged design/schedule \u2014 in deployment it is estimated from delta-v over the window, per spec.",
  "history_method": "per scored event: OrganHistory = all other-arm organ latencies for the assigned hemisphere + leave-one-out within the scored arm. Arm D organ latency = latency_from_onset_s - decider.latency_s (both logged). n=8 events/arm; indicative, not statistical.",
  "scoring_scope": "the oracle predicts TIMING feasibility only (arrival vs the v2 deadline of 2.5 s). Wrong-sign replies are a sign-discipline failure it cannot foresee and are not scored against it; they are listed per event.",
  "known_conservatism": "t_edge holds net accel constant at its observation value; the real spine's counter-tilt grows as the state develops (empirical time-to-fall was ~2.1 s/gust vs oracle t_edge ~1.6 s). History latencies are measured from gust onset while the oracle observes at +0.25 s \u2014 a further ~0.25 s of double-charged response time. Both biases push the oracle toward LET_FALL."
 },
